  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_1' aria-label=\" Dr. Ramesh versus State of Maharashtra & Anr. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('1','2026','2026_7_75_100','2026INSC635'); ><font size='4'> <strong>DR. RAMESH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>STATE OF MAHARASHTRA & ANR. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 7 S.C.R. 75</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 635</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001902026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : SANJAY KAROL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, PRASHANT KUMAR MISHRA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Matter pertains to implementation of Pre-Natal Diagnostic Techniques (Prohibition of Sex Selection) Act, 1994. Headnotes&dagger; Pre-Natal Diagnostic Techniques (Prohibition of Sex Selection) Act, 1994 &ndash; ss.20(1), 23, 4(3), 5, 6 and 29 &ndash; Authority conducted appellant and issued notice to him u/s.20(1), calling upon him to offer an explanation &ndash; Pursuant thereto, the appellant appeared before the Advisory Committee, and it was concluded that prima facie material existed in so far as the violations under PCPNDT were concerned &ndash; Suspension<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 11-06-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 3064/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('1','2026','2026_7_75_100','2026INSC635','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='